### Import a sheet: post a .xlsx bank statement in one call.
	# The BRS Dashboard's own endpoint (page/brs_dashboard/brs_import). The workbook is uploaded, read on the
	# server and handed to bulk_insert there, so the rows are never carried back and forth. What
	# comes back is bulk_insert's own answer -- "skipped", "confirmed", "inserted" and the rest,
	# exactly as above -- with the uploaded file's name added as "filename".
	#
	# Every rule above is bulk_insert's and unchanged: one Bank Account per file, the bank's own
	# order, oldest row first, reaching back far enough to include AND confirm the account's last
	# posted transaction. Importing the same sheet twice posts nothing the second time.
	#
	# The sheet's first non-empty row is the heading row, and it carries exactly these columns --
	# no more and no fewer, in any order, matched on their wording alone (case ignored, and
	# spaces, hyphens and underscores read as one):
	#   bank_account  date  description  reference_number  withdrawal  deposit  closing_balance
	# A column it does not know, or one missing or given twice, is refused. Only the workbook's
	# first sheet is read, and up to 5 MB of it (MAX_FILE_BYTES).
	#
	# Asks for create on BRS Transaction before it opens the sheet at all; bulk_insert asks again.
	#
	# The file goes up as one multipart part named "file" -- not as base64 in an argument, which a
	# statement is too large for. The path below is relative to this .rest file.
	# Full documentation: ../../page/brs_dashboard/brs_import/BRS-Import.MD
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/method/logicx_biz.logicx_hr.page.brs_dashboard.brs_import.brs_import.import_sheet
Authorization: token {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BRSImportBoundary

--BRSImportBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="HDFC-4980-April.xlsx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

< ./HDFC-4980-April.xlsx
--BRSImportBoundary--
